WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.636
-We're here with Bill Murray,
Dan Aykroyd, Ernie Hudson.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.304
You were saying,
you think Danny maybe has

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:06.439
a little too much energy.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.174
-Just on behalf of the audience,
which is a great

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.076
New York audience and
everything, you have this --

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.744
[ Cheers and applause ]
Eh, cut that crap.

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:12.945
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.280
New Yorkers don't do that.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.515
We cheer about, like --

00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:18.117
"Oh, I'm from --"
We don't do that.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.652
But we have this great
Nate Smith,

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.987
who is a fantastic drummer.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.823
And I think you would be
robbed and cheated

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.726
if you didn't get a little bit
of a just a short drum solo

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.460
from Nate Smith with Dan Aykroyd

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.496
dancing in front of Nate Smith.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.032
Wouldn't you want to hear that?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:35.268
Go ahead, Dan.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.303
[ Drum solo ]

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:13.305
-Alright.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:14.441
-Yes, sir.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.912
-Now, we need --
Just so the audi--

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:21.881
Now, Nate, you've never met
this man, correct?

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.750
-No.
-Not a planned situation.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.687
When did you --
-Nate, you're very good, too.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.656
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.591
-That is -- I mean,
that's one of the secret --

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.127
many secret hidden talents
of Dan Aykroyd.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.928
When did you know that Danny

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:39.098
was the funniest
comedy dancer of all time?

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.667
-Well, when he started going out
with this girl Rosie Shuster.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.070
The two of them were the
two worst dancers I'd ever

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.404
seen in my life.

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:48.107
They're both Canadians and
really dangerous,

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.708
and they wore
big shoes and boots.

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:51.677
And they got a lot of speed up,

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:55.047
a lot of centrifugal force
that they could not control.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.417
And so you'd have to go like,
"Okay, where are they?

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.418
Okay, good.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.719
Let's just keep moving
this way."

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.754
You'd have to sort of
counterclockwise from them

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.888
in order to not get hurt.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:04.390
-Yeah, well,
you could see there was a

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.960
sense of danger there
as we watched that.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.227
-Yeah.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.362
-You know, I think,
based on knowing your work

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:11.931
from other things
when I saw "Ghostbusters,"

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.433
I was at the age
where I was happy

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.101
that it was a film
that I could go see as a kid.

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:17.803
Was the plan from the beginning,
when you were working on it,

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.605
Dan, to make it
a kid-friendly movie?

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:23.843
-Oh, I think it was
to be a comedy for everybody.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.479
And, obviously, you know,
we watched the profanity in it.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.582
I don't think there -- There
might be one bad word in it.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.750
But, no,
we were conscious of that

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.452
and knew that we would have
a young audience.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:35.321
And, today,
we have an audience of, like,

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.189
grandchildren and
even great-grandchildren

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:38.891
of the original viewers
that are watching it.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.827
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:44.764
You all have kids.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.000
Were your kids fans of
this film?

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.370
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.
Absolutely, sure.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.805
-And I'd assume
that matters, right?

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.274
Like, I would assume
it's a huge bummer

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.875
when your kids
don't like the movie,

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.144
especially when you
make it for kids.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.446
-Well, they didn't buy
the merch.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.482
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yeah.
-But they liked the movie.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.552
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.654
It was economical
Halloween costumes.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.823
You know, "Well, I got this.
You want to wear this?

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.058
"Okay."

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.760
Yeah, they really did like it.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.164
But it was nice to have a movie
that kids could see.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.066
You know, we're not really --

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.167
You know, we just don't --
We're like you, Seth.

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.003
We don't work blue.
We don't work blue.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.671
-Thank you.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.541
Thank you for acknowledging
that in my work.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.011
We were talking backstage that
you have, over the years,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.847
met people who have tattoos
of you both from

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.981
the "Ghostbusters"
and other work.

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:37.150
And do we want to check.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.652
Anybody here have a
"Ghostbusters" tattoo?

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.653
Okay, well, it's not your night.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.721
-"Blues Brothers"?

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.557
"Blues Brothers" is another one.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.958
-And the Conehead.
I've seen him.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.126
-You've seen a Conehead?

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.561
-Is there anyone that
has a tattoo

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.264
that looks like any one of us?

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:56.335
-Tom Selleck?
Any celebrity tattoos at all?

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.305
-Nobody has Tom Selleck?
He thought Tom Selleck -- No?

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.539
No one?

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:01.841
-This is a thing.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.844
People do tattoo, you know,
famous people on their --

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.747
-You -- I heard a friend from
a story -- sorry --

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.348
a story from a
friend of ours that you were

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:11.584
on a golf course in Spain,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:15.287
and a man from
town heard you were there

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:18.358
and ran to the golf course
to show you what?

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:22.361
-To show me a tattoo
of myself on his leg.

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:26.164
Yeah. And, you know,
when a man in another language

00:04:26.164 --> 00:04:29.301
starts running at good speed at
you, you know, I'm like,

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:30.402
"I don't know.

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:31.804
How far away is he?

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:35.408
Do I hit him with a 4-iron
or do I hit him with a wedge?"

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:39.945
So -- And then I didn't know
what to say except,

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.748
"Mucho gusto."

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.284
It was -- it was -- I was happy.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.452
-I'm sure that
meant the world to him.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.288
-But, you know,
it turns out not everybody

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:53.159
in the town of Chinchón is
wearing a tattoo of myself.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.695
-He was the Bill Murray guy.
I'm sure the word got to him.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.631
Like, "You got to show up
to the golf course now."

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.832
What was it like --
Do you remember

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.201
your first experience
meeting each other?

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.837
Did you meet at Second City
or did you meet at "SNL"?

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:08.774
-Well, I had a partner,
Valri Bromfield,

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:12.378
and we had a comedy act that
we were working on,

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:15.481
like, kind of a Nichols and May
kind of improv thing.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.216
We got hired by Second City.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:20.653
And we swapped companies with
the Chicago company.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.954
The Toronto company
went down to Chicago,

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.222
and Chicago went to Toronto.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:27.326
And our guide when we arrived in
Chicago was Bill Murray,

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:30.863
who met us, took us around,
got us settled in apartments,

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.132
and showed us the grocery stores
and the local bars.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:35.935
And at that time, I think you
were in the touring company.

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:40.439
But he was -- You know,
he welcomed me to America,

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:43.676
where I got my first H-1
and my work permit.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.678
And Billy was there as
my sponsor, so...

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:46.879
-Well, that's fantastic.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.348
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:54.353
Do you -- Ernie,
do you remember the moment

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:58.257
after making this film that you
realized it was a giant hit?

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.825
Was it immediate?

00:05:59.825 --> 00:06:02.929
-No. I think, you know,
it came out, it was a hit,

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:06.131
and that was --
You know, that was what it was.

00:06:06.131 --> 00:06:10.970
But I think it was 5, 10 years
later that fans kept coming up,

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.505
kept, you know,
putting on the jumpsuits,

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:16.075
turning the cars into
Ectomobiles,

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:19.411
showing up at my house
that I realized

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:23.048
that this was something
really, really different.

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:24.850
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.619
-Well, it's incredibly special.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.253
And I really want to say
again, you know, I --

00:06:28.253 --> 00:06:30.856
Not just a film that I enjoyed,
but a film --

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.024
You know, the first one.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.593
I just really remember
the experience

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:35.427
of going to see it
in a movie theater

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:36.729
and how exciting that was.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.330
And it's really cool that
this new movie is coming out

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.565
at a time where people
can do that again.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.366
-I'm telling you,
I believe, truly,

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:43.202
that people are gonna go to
"Afterlife,"

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.536
they're going to walk in,
they're gonna see it,

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:46.405
and they're go right outside
and line up again,

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.573
just like the old days.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:50.909
That's how good it is.
[ Applause ]

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:54.413
-Does it -- I know you've been
back in the building,

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:57.216
but is it --
Do you have old flashbacks

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:59.218
coming back to 30 Rock?

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:02.221
-Yeah, I remember
sneaking in and out

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.689
of this building all the time.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.291
You know,
you'd try to avoid someone

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.592
that would make you go to work

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:09.294
or someone that was trying to
grab you after work.

00:07:09.294 --> 00:07:12.030
I knew all the secret exits
out of this place.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:17.003
And now when I walk down
the halls, I think,

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:18.170
"There's no one
following you, Bill.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:21.406
You're okay. You're safe."

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:23.141
-We made it clear --
And I want to stress this.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:25.043
We made it clear
with all security,

00:07:25.043 --> 00:07:27.546
"Mr. Murray
is not to be followed.

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:29.014
By his request."

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:30.550
I can't tell the
three of you how much

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.651
it means that you
spent time with us today.

00:07:32.651 --> 00:07:33.719
Thank you so much
for being here.

